[33:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that lower resolution images generate faster. So here\'s how the system works. First, it generates the image at low resolution. And then upscales that image and then it adds a tiny bit of noise and lets the original image model spend only'

[33:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'one final highresolution step cleaning up these details. Think of it like doing a rough sketch on a small piece of paper, then enlarging it, then spending just a minute sharpening the fine'

[33:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'details instead of drawing the entire huge picture from scratch. So, here are some of its generations. You can see the detail and quality are still very good and the results are extremely impressive. So get this. For Zimage'

[33:52] [scene:talk]
