VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different types of robot models with different hands. So, the key idea from Cord is to represent the demonstration in terms of forces and torqus applied to the object. Then it trains the robot to create a similar effect even if the'

[36:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'robot is built differently. It uses this contact guidance data and reinforcement learning to train robot policies on how to use objects. And this is very versatile. It works on different types of objects, especially articulated'

